The '''Giju Run''' was a [[hyperspace route]]<ref name="NoP" /> with one terminus at the [[Giju system]]<ref name="GM" /> of [[Herglic Space]] in the [[Colonies]]<ref name="HerglicSpace" /> and [[the Interior]].<ref name="Interior" /> Running along the border of the Colonies and the [[Core Worlds]],<ref name="GM" /> the route then passed through the planet [[Bardotta]] in the [[Shasos sector]]'s [[Bardotta system]],<ref name="NoP" /> the [[Zardossa Stix system]], and the [[Deymasoll system]]&mdash;all in the Colonies&mdash;and then terminated at the [[Kitel Phard system]]<ref name="GM" /> of the [[Atrisian Commonwealth]]<ref name="Atrisian" /> in the Core Worlds. THe Giju system acted as a junction from the route onto the [[Rimma Trade Route]]<ref name="GM" /> and the [[Herglic Alley]].<ref name="HerglicAlley" /> The Giju Run passed through [[Standard Galactic Grid]] squares L-13, K-13, J-13, and J-12.<ref name="GM" />

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Starcruiserdate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]] to [[34 ABY]].</ref> the route was included on a partial [[Star map|map]] of the [[galaxy]] displayed on screens on board [[Chandrila Star Line]]'s [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|Star Cruiser]] ''[[Halcyon]]'' while it traveled from the Core Worlds' [[Chandrila system]] to the Outer Rim Territories.<ref name="GS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Giju Run was first pictured in "[[Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Star Wars: The Force Awakens?|Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''?]]," an article written by [[Mark Newbold]] and published on [[StarWars.com]] on [[January 29]], [[2016]].<ref name="WhereTFA">{{SW|url=news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-star-wars-the-force-awakens|text=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''?|int=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Star Wars: The Force Awakens?}}</ref> It was then identified in ''[[Nexus of Power]]'', a ''[[Star Wars Roleplaying]]'' supplement published by [[Fantasy Flight Games]]<ref name="NoP" /> on [[March 17]], 2016.<ref name="Places of Power">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2016/3/17/places-of-power|text=Places of Power|date=2016-03-17}}</ref>

The route then appeared [[in-universe]] for the first time when it was depicted on a map viewable in [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], an immersive roleplaying experience at [[W:c:disney:Walt Disney World Resort|Walt Disney World Resort]] in Florida<ref name="GS" /> that opened to the public on [[March 1]], [[2022]],<ref name="31 Things">{{SW|url=news/31-things-we-learned-about-star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=31 Things We Learned in an Exclusive Preview of ''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser|nolive=1}}</ref> and had its final voyage from [[September 28]] to [[September 30|30]], [[2023]].<ref name="StarcruiserClosure">{{Disney|subdomain=disneyworld|domain=go.com|url=destinations/star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser}}</ref> The [[Giju Run/Legends|Giju Run]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned in the ''[[Player's Guide to Tapani]]'', a [[1997]] supplement for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'' written by [[Paul Sudlow]] and [[Eric S. Trautmann]] and published by [[West End Games]].<ref name="Tapani">''[[Player's Guide to Tapani]]''</ref>

